# Known Failure Patterns in This Codebase

Before role-playing the review board, scan the spec/diff specifically for these — they are not hypothetical; each has already caused a real, shipped bug in this app, and the same shape of mistake is the single most likely way a new feature breaks here too.

- **Synchronous side effects blocking the response.** Any `Mail::send()`, `broadcast()`, outbound HTTP call, or third-party SDK call that runs directly in a controller method — not wrapped in the established `dispatch(fn () => ...)->afterResponse()` idiom — can turn an unrelated failure (a bad SMTP config, a slow API) into a 500 on an otherwise-successful action. This exact bug shipped once already: a synchronous `Mail::send()` in an admin controller 500'd requests even after the primary DB write and broadcast had already succeeded.
- **Malformed Eloquent eager-load calls.** `Model::load('a', ['b' => fn ($q) => ...])` (mixing a bare string arg with a constrained-relation array across *separate* arguments) silently mis-parses — it must be one array: `load(['a', 'b' => fn ($q) => ...])`. This exact mistake shipped once and crashed a whole page with an opaque "Method name must be a string" error.
- **New admin routes missing from `AdminPermissions::SECTIONS`.** If a route name isn't in the map, the permission middleware treats it as unrestricted, not "deny by default." Every new `admin.*` route in the diff needs a matching section entry (new or existing) checked off explicitly.
- **Global page-level JS silently fighting new AJAX code.** This app has a global capture-phase `document` listener that shows a full-screen loading overlay on *every* form submit unless the form opts out with `data-no-loading-overlay` — new AJAX-driven forms that forget this opt-out get a stuck "Processing…" overlay with no way to dismiss it, since it only clears on real navigation.
- **Badges/counts computed once at page render, never live-updated.** Sidebar unread counts, list-row timestamps, and similar server-rendered-once values do not refresh themselves after an in-page action (marking read, a Pusher event, an AJAX update) unless explicit JS is written to patch that specific DOM node. Assume every such value is stale-by-default and demand the spec says how/when it's corrected.
- **N+1s hidden inside Blade loops calling model helper methods.** e.g. `$project->unreadClientChatMessagesCount()` invoked once per row in a `@foreach` runs one query per row with no obvious "N+1" shape in the controller — these hide in the view layer here, not just the controller.
- **Two nearly-identical Portal/Admin controller pairs for the same feature drifting apart.** This app consistently mirrors a feature into a `Portal\XController` and an `Admin\XController` (chat, uploads, support tickets). Check that authorization, validation limits, and side effects (notifications, emails, broadcasts) were actually mirrored, not just the happy path.

