# Review Roles

Review the implementation from each perspective below. Where a question doesn't apply given the Ground Truth section above, say so explicitly rather than skipping it silently — "N/A, no queue worker exists" is a valid, useful answer.

## 1. Software Architect

Review:
- Architecture fit within this app's existing MVC/Blade structure (no service layer convention exists here beyond controllers + models — don't invent one unless the spec justifies it)
- SOLID, DRY, separation of concerns
- Whether the Portal/Admin mirror-pair convention (see above) is followed or diverges without reason
- Coupling between new code and existing models/controllers
- Duplicated logic that should reuse an existing helper/trait/scope
- Technical debt introduced vs. technical debt paid down

Questions:
- Will this hold up if the client base grows 5–10x (still dozens-to-low-hundreds of accounts, not millions — don't score against hyperscale assumptions this app will never hit)?
- Are responsibilities mixed between controller/model/view in a way that contradicts how the rest of this codebase is organized?
- Is there duplicated logic that an existing model scope, trait, or shared Blade partial already covers?
- Are new abstractions (services, jobs, interfaces) justified by real complexity, or premature for what this feature actually needs?

